      "challenges": [
        "1,924 alerts; 1,892 verified (98.3%), 321 validated suspects, 315 investigated (98.1%), and 170 transferred. Six provinces have numeric alert rows (Haut-Uele, Bas-Uele, Ituri, Nord-Kivu, Sud-Ubangi and Tshopo); Sud-Kivu is unavailable, not zero.",
        "Nord-Kivu prints 351 hospitalised patients, 271 in normed structures and a 70.9% occupancy rate without a bed count. SR133 and SR135 print 354 beds, and 271/354 is 76.6%; 70.9% equals SR133's own 251/354, and would need 382 beds here. The rate is withheld as a conflict. The care challenges repeat SR133's 31.2% of patients outside normed structures, while SR134's own figures give 80/351 (22.8%); no bed is available in Butembo or Katwa.",
        "Contact follow-up 23,364/30,018 (77.8%). Six reporting province rows sum to the national contact line; Sud-Kivu is unavailable, not zero. The national rate moved from 79.2% the day before, and no province followed all of its contacts.",
        "PoE/PoC completeness is 97/99 (98.0%). The Avakubi PoC is closed for insecurity; screening refusals are high at Nzebi (46%) and Pluto (32%); alert entry in DHIS2 Tracker and team mobility are weak in Rwampara, Nizi and Bunia; threats against PoC staff persist on the Butembo axis.",
        "Ituri CTE/CT suspect areas are saturated in Nizi, Mambasa, Lolwa, Kilo, Mangala and Mandima.",
        "Tshopo remains out of frozen ERVEBO doses after a doctor died on 24 September; 500 thawed doses were redirected to Buta. Four swabs failed in Beni after an incident at Katula cemetery."
      ],
